  "id": "DrugBank_DB01388 - MONDO_5044",
  "verbalization": "Mibefradil is associated with Hypertensive Disorder through a chain of indications that link it to Hypertension and then to the Disorder. The evidence suggests that Mibefradil may be repurposed for hypertension, with multiple drugs (Xipamide, Rilmenidine, and Trimazosin) sharing a common indication of treating hypertension, which in turn is linked to Hypertensive Disorder. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, suggesting that Mibefradil may be considered a potential candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Hypertensive Disorder. The overlapping pathways highlight the role of antihypertensive medications in the development of the Disorder, reinforcing the likelihood of a repurposing effect. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of targeting the underlying mechanisms of hypertension to address the Disorder.",
